From: MahanHD <mahanheidari2003@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/a3xx: run kgsl's power-on fixup after every power-on

The downstream kgsl driver runs a short compute dispatch on every a3xx
before the first submission after each power-on, to set up the shader
processor after power collapse ("Some targets require a special
workaround shader to be executed after power-collapse"). The stock
kernel of the Xperia Z1 Compact has it too. drm/msm never ran it.

Emit the same commands, in the same order, right after CP_ME_INIT, which
runs on every hw_init: at power-on, on runtime resume and after a GPU
reset. Like kgsl, turn register protection off around it, since it
writes RBBM_CLOCK_CTL. The 491 dwords are identical to what kgsl's
adreno_a3xx_pwron_fixup_init() generates, and the shader to the copy in
the stock kernel binary.

---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a3xx_gpu.c	2026-10-08 23:48:53.731041770 +0400
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a3xx_gpu.c	2026-10-08 23:49:46.309805758 +0400
@@ -82,6 +82,286 @@
 	adreno_flush(gpu, ring, REG_AXXX_CP_RB_WPTR);
 }
 
+/*
+ * The a3xx power-on fixup of the downstream kgsl driver
+ * (adreno_a3xx_pwron_fixup_init()): "Some targets require a special
+ * workaround shader to be executed after power-collapse". kgsl, and the
+ * stock kernel of the Xperia Z1 Compact, run it on every a3xx before the
+ * first submission after each power-on. It is a small compute dispatch over
+ * the shader processor. The commands are kgsl's, in kgsl's order; the shader
+ * matches the stock kernel's byte for byte.
+ */
